  "feedback": "The anatomical ellipsoid approach gives a recognizable standing figure, and the staggered gather arc genuinely channels Mutu's collage-assembly feeling — strong concept-to-form mapping. The earth palette is excellent. Two improvements: (1) the 18 overlapping ellipsoids will read as a soft pointillist mannequin rather than torn collage patches — consider using flat polygon quads or triangulated Voronoi cells instead of individual particles so the 'torn paper' materiality comes through, and (2) the edge shimmer is too subtle to convey patch boundaries; sharper alpha falloff at patch borders (step function rather than smoothstep) and slight z-offset between adjacent patches would sell the layered-collage depth that defines Mutu's surface."
